{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And she also.</b> Written with a yod." "<b>And she</b> — in Abraham's presence; <b>also she</b> — not in his presence." "<b>I did this.</b> That I took her. Another interpretation: that I did not approach her. One may say that because he examined her, HaShem reproved him and did not strike him, but Pharaoh, who did not examine, was struck."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {2 "בדק appears twice with different senses: Abraham 'examined/tested' (the situation), Pharaoh 'did not examine' — i.e., acted without investigation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:02.424410490Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}